   773430,
   5195
  ],
  "…Ha. HA! Since ’03. Since the LIGHTS WENT OUT. And it took you two — a route-runner and the partner who grew up along the whole road. Look at the ringer, children. Look at him. He’s SMILING. I have known that man thirty years and seen it twice.": [
   778875,
   12085
  ],
  "Then hear the last of it. You didn’t just beat a table tonight. You made it OUT. The porch, the corner, the basement, my room — those are behind you now, and they stay yours. What’s ahead is the other game. The ranked rooms. The televised tables. The league with its numbers and its lights.": [
   791210,
   15600
  ],
  "Go be professional at them, little one. That world grades everything and forgives nothing, and it has no idea what the block sent it. …Dee. When they ask where you learned — and they WILL ask — say the route. Say it proud.": [
   807060,
   11230
  ],
  "And Dee. Your daddy’s name is spoken kindly on every table of this route again. You did that. Not the crown — YOU. Now go home and call your mama before the street does. Champions first. Stories after.": [
   818540,
   11855
  ],
  "Close isn’t a crown. But it is closer than most ever stand, and I do not say that to be kind — I have forgotten how to be kind about cards.": [
   830645,
   8290
  ],
  "My table keeps a chair for you. Both chairs. Earn them again — I will be here, being bored a little less than I was. That is your doing too.": [
   839185,
   11545
  ],
  "Back at my table. I told the ringer you would be. He did not bet against me — he remembers ’09, the last time he did.": [
   850980,
   6335
  ],
  "Then tonight begins where tonight should. No speeches — mine or yours. The cards have been patient. So have I. Less than the cards, more than I expected.": [
   857565,
   9630
  ],
  "A third sitting. In twenty-two years, three parties have sat three times. One took a single game off the streak and tells it like a crown. …I respect the three of you equally. That is not a compliment I rehearse.": [
   867445,
   10665
  ],
  "So I did. A king’s words return to him like weather. Deal, old friend. Let us finish the conversation the route started.": [
   878360,
   7830
  ],
  "The champions return to the room they took. It does not get less strange, saying it. It gets better.": [
   886440,
   7050
  ],
  "Then it is a table of holders, and the crown sits in the middle like a guest. Play, champions. Defending is the second education. I was an excellent student of it — out of necessity, and loneliness. You will be neither. That is my blessing, and it is also a warning.": [
   893740,
   16125
  ],
  "One hand. …Interesting. The ringer just adjusted in his seat. He has adjusted in his seat eleven times since 2003. The room will discuss it for a year.": [
   910115,
   9545
  ],
  "Ahead. At my table. Against the streak. …Do you hear that sound, children? Neither do I. That’s the block, holding its breath, twenty years deep.": [
   919910,
   9185
  ],
  "The king leads, as the king has led since the lights went out. It is not arrogance at this point. It is archive.": [
   929345,
   6355
  ],
  "A nil. Against ME. …In 2007 a man tried that here and the story still gets told in Coleman’s shop like a ghost tale. Finish it or join the telling, friend. I’m honestly curious — and I am never curious.": [
   935950,
   11970
  ],
  "Match point. Against the undefeated. Understand me, both of you: I will not insult this moment by going easy. Whatever you take tonight, you take at full price, from the real thing.": [
   948170,
   11485
  ],
  "The final hand. Twenty-two years I waited in this room for a game that deserved one. …Play it like the story it already is.": [
   959905,
   7390
  ],
  "Their hand. …The ringer is looking at me. He has not looked at me during a game in nine years. Whatever this is, it has his attention. It has mine.": [
   967545,
   10700
  ],
  "Mine. As the archive expected. And yet the ringer remains seated forward. Interesting archives, these.": [
   978495,
   8455
  ],
  "The first hand of the return. No speeches live here anymore. Only the rest of the story.": [
   987200,
   4635
  ],
  "The first look. Twenty-two years of first looks at this table… and I still Lean in for this one. That should tell you something.": [
   992085,
   7280
  ],
  "A real bid. At last, a table that speaks in numbers instead of hopes. Continue.": [
   999615,
   6895
  ],
  "The joker. At my table, that card has started and ended dynasties. Play it like you know that.": [
   1006760,
   6505
  ],
  "Cut. …The ringer shifted again. Twice in one game. The archive is being REWRITTEN tonight, whatever the score says.": [
   1013515,
   7035
  ],
  "The nil that died earlier in this game — I keep it in mind. Kings keep everything in mind. It is the entire job description.": [
   1020800,
   7755
  ],
  "After that swing, the ringer looked at ME for instruction. I gave none. Some games must be allowed to become what they are.": [
   1028805,
   7715
  ],
  "You return. Good. Unfinished games are the only appointments I keep twice.": [
   1036770,
   4100
  ],
  "The ringer heard that. So did I. Reasons are cards too, little one — and you just played yours face up, at my table, without flinching. Whatever happens next, THAT was champion’s work.": [
   1041120,
   9325
  ],
  "Look at your rail, children. EVERYBODY came. The whole route, standing in my yard. They didn’t come to see ME. …Win or lose — what happens here tonight gets told on every porch on this block. For years.": [
   1050695,
   12610
  ],
  "Then feed them well, Pat. Whatever’s left of us.": [
   1063555,
   2570
  ],
  "One win. …There. Now it sits where everybody can see it: you ain’t won yet. One is a story people tell. Two — back to back — is a crown.": [
   1066375,
   10015
  ],
  "Double or nothing — that is still the wording. Run it back and take everything. Lose, and you were never here.": [
   1076640,
   6555
  ],
  "There it is. One win is a story you tell other people. Two is a crown. You have the story.": [
   1083445,
   7080
  ],
  "My door stays open. Kings can wait. The question, as ever, is whether you can.": [
   1090775,
   4755
  ],
  "Frederick Douglass. Taught himself to read when it was forbidden to him, escaped slavery at twenty, and wrote it all down for the world to answer for.": [
   1095780,
   7745
  ],
  "Harriet Tubman. She got herself free — then went back some thirteen times for family and strangers alike, and she brought out every single one.": [
   1103775,
   9100
  ],
  "Nat Turner. In 1831 he rose in Southampton County and led the deadliest slave rebellion in American history.": [
   1113125,
   7955
  ],
  "Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Twenty-six years old when Montgomery stopped riding the buses — and he led that boycott all 381 days.": [
   1121330,
   7965
  ],
  "Sojourner Truth. Born enslaved — and the first Black woman to win a court case against a white man in this country, bringing her own son home.": [
   1129545,
   9535
  ],
  "Fannie Lou Hamer. A Mississippi sharecropper who stood before a national convention in 1964 and told the truth until the whole country had to listen.": [
   1139330,
   10580
  ],
  "Marcus Garvey. He built the largest Black movement of his age — and put our own ships on the water with the Black Star Line.": [
   1150160,
   7445
  ],
  "Ida B. Wells. A mob wrecked her newspaper office for printing the truth about lynching — so she carried that truth north and printed it louder.": [
   1157855,
   9430
  ],
  "W.E.B. Du Bois. The first Black man to earn a Ph.D. from Harvard, in 1895 — and he spent ninety-five years writing the record straight.": [
   1167535,
   7820
  ],
  "Malcolm X. He remade himself in a prison cell — walked out teaching discipline, dignity, and standing up straight.": [
   1175605,
   6665
  ],
  "Angela Davis. A philosopher they put on trial in 1972 — she walked out acquitted, and she has been teaching ever since.": [
   1182520,
   8935
  ],
  "Huey P. Newton. In 1966, in Oakland, he co-founded the Black Panther Party — and a neighborhood's protection became a movement.": [
   1191705,
   8260
  ],
  "Hold on now. That's Malcolm they just cut. The man told us freedom would come 'by any means necessary' — a spade on a playing card changes none of it.": [
   1200215,
   10035
  ],
  "Malcolm X, cut down on a trick. He taught a whole generation to stand up straight — 'by any means necessary' was never a slogan. It was a promise.": [
   1210500,
   8345
  ]
 }
